    "body": "## Purpose\n\nConnect real DUNCAN/Letta runtime events to the existing SHERIFF V1 JetStream path. This is a producer bridge only: no second SHERIFF, daemon, broker, policy engine, or host-published internal port.\n\n## Boundary\n\n- `turn_start` publishes `zb.agent.task.started`.\n- Tool/provider errors publish factual operation-level `FAIL` observations only.\n- No prompt, tool arguments/output, model output, or raw Letta IDs are persisted.\n- Exact Letta agent identity is required; stable IDs are HMAC-pseudonymized.\n- Queue, payload, publish timeout, and active child process are bounded.\n- Agent-callable and automatic PASS are absent.\n- NATS remains Compose-internal through the existing worker container.\n\n## Fresh evidence\n\n- SHERIFF tests: 66/66 PASS.\n- `scripts/sheriff_validate.py`: PASS.\n- `scripts/hq_validate.py`: PASS.\n- Node TypeScript syntax check: PASS.\n- Physical owner-PC proof: one real OpenAI/Letta DUNCAN turn increased `source=zb://letta/duncan` ledger count by exactly 1.\n- Persisted event had pseudonymous subject and contained no raw agent or conversation ID.\n- SHERIFF stack status: all required services running, blocker NONE.\n- Mod diagnostics after probe: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n\n## Review correction\n\nAn initial local-only candidate exposed an unsafe self-issued PASS tool. Independent review caught it; the tool was removed before this commit. The committed bridge cannot construct PASS.\n\n## Known separate boundary\n\nThis PR proves real DUNCAN event ingestion. Policy-complete portable incident verdict export to `hq/sheriff/verdicts/` remains a separate gate before runtime incident verdicts can be treated as durable repository authority.\n\nMERGE = NO unless separately authorized.",
